      origins: 'Tressette originated in Italy and is first recorded from the early 18th century; its lack of trumps suggests it may be older. It is one of Italy\'s major national card games alongside Scopa and Briscola. The name may derive from "Tre Sett" (three sevens): Cäsar (1800) states that a player holding three sevens could declare and win. The game spread to former Italian-influenced regions including Albania, Montenegro, coastal Slovenia and Croatia, and the Canton of Ticino; the Austrian game Trischettn in South Tyrol is a derivative.',
